WHY THE TWO HALVES DIFFER

  The tool that most people install — @kiberos/claude-max-proxy — is
  published as readable source under the MIT license and stays that way:
  what you run, you can read. This package is the engine underneath it. It
  is distributed as a compiled bundle because the decisions inside it (how a
  prompt cache is kept warm, when a spend is stopped, how sessions and
  tokens are kept apart) are the substance of the product, not its plumbing.
  You may use it without paying and without asking. You may not take it
  apart or hand it on.

